{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Do not slander</b> — In this verse he warned against talebearing, and he mentioned the slave who flees, for it is more severe than all talebearing." "<b>Do not slander</b> — Do not expose him and make him known with your tongue, and he is a slave who flees from the nations to the land of Israel to convert, that they should not return him to his master, as it is said: he shall dwell with you in your land." "<b>A slave to his master</b> — Both of them are not upright, as in the matter of 'you shall not surrender a slave to his master,' and there it mentioned that he should not inform against him to his master." "<b>and you bear guilt</b> — And you have already borne guilt because he fled to you for the honor of HaShem, to take refuge under His wings."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:32.511387313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}